NAME
    tilemap - decode a grid of tilemap entries as text

SYNOPSIS
    tilemap <space> <addr> <cols> <rows>

DESCRIPTION
    Decodes a <cols> by <rows> grid of tilemap or nametable entries
    starting at <addr> in memory space <space>, printing one core-
    formatted label per cell. Numeric arguments are parsed as hex.

    The caller supplies the exact base address (for example, from BG1SC or
    equivalent registers in regs(1)); 'tilemap' does not resolve
    background-layer register mappings automatically.

EXAMPLES
    tilemap VRAM 0 20 20

EXIT STATUS
    0   Tilemap grid printed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, unknown space, invalid argument, or session
        service fault.

SEE ALSO
    tile(1), pal(1), sprites(1), regs(1), mem(1), spaces(1)
